1
00:01:22,919 --> 00:01:27,419
Normally I drive across the
market square. But we have to wait.

2
00:01:31,759 --> 00:01:34,919
Have a nice day! Is
that the getaway car?

3
00:01:35,199 --> 00:01:38,239
Getaway... A shot! Quick!

4
00:01:42,279 --> 00:01:46,779
The helicopter has already
taken off. One moment please!

5
00:01:47,639 --> 00:01:49,879
When do we storm it?
- In 10 minutes.

6
00:01:50,159 --> 00:01:54,659
In 10 minutes the heli
lands. Don't lose your nerve!

7
00:01:57,959 --> 00:02:01,319
I'll give you exactly five!
- Asshole!

8
00:02:01,599 --> 00:02:06,099
Mr. Stich! Forgive me! Lessing!
I'm the new one from Hamburg.

9
00:02:08,439 --> 00:02:10,639
Already? What's going on here?

10
00:02:10,919 --> 00:02:15,319
A maniac wants a
million, a heli and a pizza.

11
00:02:15,599 --> 00:02:20,099
A hostage is dead. Officer Dorn
is now his exchange hostage.

12
00:02:21,919 --> 00:02:25,399
Who?
Kira Dorn. He wanted a woman.

13
00:02:25,679 --> 00:02:28,999
The SWAT team needs 10 more minutes.

14
00:02:29,279 --> 00:02:31,999
Here's the pizza!
- Thanks, Steffen!

15
00:02:32,279 --> 00:02:34,239
Who's bringing it in?

16
00:02:36,039 --> 00:02:38,399
Are you sure? Give me your phone!

17
00:02:43,359 --> 00:02:47,039
Call me in three minutes!

18
00:02:55,279 --> 00:02:59,779
* Suspenseful music *

19
00:03:16,039 --> 00:03:20,519
Two minutes ago, they said the
helicopter was in the air.

20
00:03:20,799 --> 00:03:25,159
And now you're bringing a pizza.
You want to storm in!

21
00:03:25,439 --> 00:03:29,939
Not with a pregnant hostage!
Then we're safe for a while.

22
00:03:31,319 --> 00:03:35,519
Is everything okay?
The doctor says yes.

23
00:03:35,799 --> 00:03:40,299
What is it going to be?
It doesn't matter. As long as it's a healthy boy.

24
00:03:40,919 --> 00:03:45,419
Can you guys shut up?
He's hungry.

25
00:03:45,999 --> 00:03:50,499
* The phone rings. *

26
00:03:56,639 --> 00:03:59,639
Yes. Yes.

27
00:04:01,119 --> 00:04:04,359
Hold on! It's for you.

28
00:04:10,599 --> 00:04:13,599
You despicable coward!
A pregnant woman!

29
00:04:14,599 --> 00:04:16,919
Hans is lying. We're getting out.

30
00:04:24,439 --> 00:04:28,079
Was that a drill?
What did you think?

31
00:04:29,239 --> 00:04:32,559
Oh! Excuse me!

32
00:04:33,439 --> 00:04:37,199
Lessing.
Hans Bangen. Not that bad.

33
00:04:38,079 --> 00:04:41,399
I didn't know about you.
Me neither.

34
00:04:41,679 --> 00:04:46,179
Extra cheese! That's awesome!
Yummy! Stop eating that crap all the time!

35
00:04:49,919 --> 00:04:53,959
So yummy!
Are you keeping up?

36
00:05:04,479 --> 00:05:08,979
A slice of pizza, Lessing?
You should have briefed me!

37
00:05:09,599 --> 00:05:14,079
One in three officers didn't
know that it was a drill.

38
00:05:14,359 --> 00:05:17,879
Realistic. Is that
different in Hamburg?

39
00:05:18,159 --> 00:05:23,465
I know what realistic looks like! 
I wouldn't send a pregnant woman.

40
00:05:23,759 --> 00:05:27,479
Who knows? Why does
she work in the field?

41
00:05:27,759 --> 00:05:32,259
She works until the contractions start.
She doesn't let anyone hold her back.

42
00:05:40,279 --> 00:05:42,839
This has to stay between us.

43
00:05:43,119 --> 00:05:47,619
He had mental health
problems in Hamburg. Burnout.

44
00:05:49,399 --> 00:05:53,899
KDD. Brutal job. Very
few stick with it for long.

45
00:05:54,679 --> 00:05:59,179
Handle him with care!
We'll get him back on his feet.

46
00:06:00,599 --> 00:06:05,099
Colleagues! All in all,
it was pretty decent.

47
00:06:08,599 --> 00:06:13,079
Cordon: flawless. Communication
with the citizen: good.

48
00:06:13,359 --> 00:06:17,859
But, Steffen, the pizza from
Mykonos was an unnecessary risk.

49
00:06:19,959 --> 00:06:24,319
Next time: Mario! Thank you!

50
00:06:40,479 --> 00:06:44,979
If that's going too fast for you,
no problem. Just get here first!

51
00:06:46,199 --> 00:06:50,699
No! We're looking for a gang that
steals toilet paper from the town hall.

52
00:06:51,479 --> 00:06:55,439
And someone who smears
cars with ground meat.

53
00:06:55,719 --> 00:06:57,719
It was human ground meat!

54
00:07:00,759 --> 00:07:05,079
Mrs. Dorn! Can you come down?
What's going on?

55
00:07:05,359 --> 00:07:09,859
He was standing in the Poseck garden.
Since last night. Come take a look!

56
00:07:11,479 --> 00:07:14,039
That looks like blood.

57
00:07:14,319 --> 00:07:18,819
Who is it registered to?
Brigitte Hoppe, handbag in front.

58
00:07:21,239 --> 00:07:25,719
Hans, come down and bring
the blacklight lamp with you!

59
00:07:28,319 --> 00:07:32,819
Brigitte Hoppe is the Sausage
Queen. Butcher shop with six branches.

60
00:07:33,639 --> 00:07:37,479
They make the best
Thuringian, Fat Hoppe.

61
00:07:37,759 --> 00:07:42,259
She's not that fat at all. That's
what the sausage is called.

62
00:07:44,759 --> 00:07:45,799
Ah, I see.

63
00:07:51,559 --> 00:07:53,679
That was quite a scratch.

64
00:07:54,759 --> 00:07:57,959
That is definitely
blood. How much?

65
00:07:58,239 --> 00:08:02,199
It needs to be extracted
first. But there's a lot.

66
00:08:05,359 --> 00:08:09,859
A female butcher deals with blood.
Could she be the ground meat perpetrator?

67
00:08:11,599 --> 00:08:16,099
She doesn't leave a handbag
behind. How tall is she?

68
00:08:19,119 --> 00:08:23,079
1.63 meters. For that,
the seat is too far back.

69
00:08:44,639 --> 00:08:49,139
Sigmar Hoppe is the
son and junior director.

70
00:08:49,559 --> 00:08:54,059
I bet, other than the mother, no woman
has ever been in the house. Sausage!

71
00:08:59,919 --> 00:09:04,419
Lessing. Dorn. Criminal
Police. Can we come in?

72
00:09:05,119 --> 00:09:07,079
Yes.

73
00:09:20,159 --> 00:09:24,659
That's great! Where is that?
In Heilbad Heiligenstadt.

74
00:09:26,479 --> 00:09:30,839
Did you do this? 
Do you think that's too far-fetched?

75
00:09:31,119 --> 00:09:34,759
Good morning! Hello!

76
00:09:35,039 --> 00:09:39,539
Mrs. Reuter! Then let
me get you out quickly.

77
00:09:40,039 --> 00:09:41,519
Yes.

78
00:09:43,279 --> 00:09:46,479
I doubt your
little-sausage theory.

79
00:09:48,399 --> 00:09:52,039
Is your mother at home?
Hold on!

80
00:09:52,319 --> 00:09:56,819
Mom! Oh! She's
probably already at work.

81
00:09:58,879 --> 00:10:03,379
No. And her cell phone is off too.
When did you last see your mother?

82
00:10:04,119 --> 00:10:07,799
Last evening at the
office. Can I help you?

83
00:10:08,079 --> 00:10:12,579
It's possible that something
happened to your mother.

84
00:10:12,919 --> 00:10:17,419
We found her car at Poseck's
Garden. Her handbag was inside.

85
00:10:18,759 --> 00:10:22,559
Strange!
There's blood in the trunk.

86
00:10:26,039 --> 00:10:27,719
Mom!

87
00:10:32,239 --> 00:10:36,739
She's a hunter. I don't know
what she's been driving around for.

88
00:10:40,759 --> 00:10:44,119
There was also an
axe in the car. This size.

89
00:10:44,399 --> 00:10:48,359
Mother always
butchers the pigs herself.

90
00:10:48,639 --> 00:10:51,839
Can we head upstairs?
Yes.

91
00:10:52,119 --> 00:10:56,519
Don't touch anything! She notices
everything and then she'll kill me.

92
00:11:08,639 --> 00:11:13,139
Meat-nose?
Yeah, from the cold storage. Unpleasant.

93
00:11:13,679 --> 00:11:18,179
Did your mother have any plans yesterday?
Not that I know of.

94
00:11:18,599 --> 00:11:23,099
She often has appointments off-site, but was
looking forward to watching "Tatort" on Sunday.

95
00:11:25,199 --> 00:11:29,699
Then she must have been at home.
Probably. I went to bed early.

96
00:11:36,439 --> 00:11:40,939
* A football match is being broadcast loudly
on the TV. *

97
00:11:45,679 --> 00:11:50,179
You would have noticed that.
Sorry!

98
00:11:53,159 --> 00:11:56,359
We need something for
the DNA comparison.

99
00:11:56,639 --> 00:11:59,959
With the blood in the trunk.
Exactly.

100
00:12:09,359 --> 00:12:13,859
It's working again. Are we done?
Everything will come to light.

101
00:12:15,319 --> 00:12:19,559
Are you also driving
your mother's car?

102
00:12:19,839 --> 00:12:23,039
No. I don't understand the question.

103
00:12:23,319 --> 00:12:26,759
We're worried about
your mother. Aren't you?

104
00:12:27,039 --> 00:12:31,539
Blood, hatchet, handbag!
This doesn't seem to worry you.

105
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:35,719
Thank God! There she is!
Mom, something's going on here.

106
00:12:37,319 --> 00:12:41,819
Who's there? I can barely
understand you. Please speak louder!

107
00:12:45,439 --> 00:12:49,939
Where? How much? In two hours? What?

108
00:12:52,359 --> 00:12:53,759
Hello!

109
00:12:54,879 --> 00:12:59,379
Hello! My mother has been kidnapped. I
am supposed to pay a ransom. No police!

110
00:13:01,519 --> 00:13:06,019
Was that a man or a woman? 
Don't know. The voice was distorted.

111
00:13:07,639 --> 00:13:11,839
Do you have any idea
who it might have been?

112
00:13:12,119 --> 00:13:16,619
No. She gets along with
everyone. That's nonsense.

113
00:13:19,999 --> 00:13:24,159
Her husband pulled the strings
and she handled the money.

114
00:13:24,439 --> 00:13:28,939
The Hoppes own real estate. She
canceled her contract with a daycare.

115
00:13:30,359 --> 00:13:34,859
She doesn't help the Weimar Food Bank
either, because it's not tax-deductible.

116
00:13:36,079 --> 00:13:39,079
And the butcher shops
are still running fine?

117
00:13:39,359 --> 00:13:42,759
You haven't tried a
fat Hoppe yet!

118
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:54,079
You know your mother's
reputation. No, I don't!

119
00:13:54,359 --> 00:13:58,599
Instead of a heart ...
she has just a purse?

120
00:13:58,879 --> 00:14:02,319
And many enemies. Do
you absolutely have no idea?

121
00:14:02,599 --> 00:14:05,999
The money must be at
Theater Square in 2 hours.

122
00:14:06,279 --> 00:14:10,779
That's too much for you. Your
father died last week. Our condolences.

123
00:14:12,279 --> 00:14:13,919
Yes.

124
00:14:14,199 --> 00:14:18,699
Is the kidnapping related to that? 
It's all happening in very quick succession.

125
00:14:19,599 --> 00:14:24,099
Kidnappings end all the
better, the higher the ransom is.

126
00:14:27,319 --> 00:14:31,819
How much was demanded?
45,000 euros.

127
00:14:35,519 --> 00:14:38,479
That's a lot of money
for many people.

128
00:14:39,959 --> 00:14:42,199
We'll take care of everything.

129
00:14:52,959 --> 00:14:57,459
Who's playing the couple? Mandy, Rocco,
can you bring yourselves to go through with it?

130
00:14:59,759 --> 00:15:04,199
Is that right? Exchange,
Theaterplatz, in the trash can?

131
00:15:04,479 --> 00:15:08,759
In two hours. Nadine
Reuter was at Sigmar Hoppe's.

132
00:15:09,039 --> 00:15:13,539
On her scooter. She stayed over at his
place; in front of us they used the formal "you."

133
00:15:13,959 --> 00:15:15,839
Lecko mio!

134
00:15:16,119 --> 00:15:19,199
Can we go to the theater?
I'm up next!

135
00:15:19,479 --> 00:15:23,439
What about Ms. Reuter,
besides what's obvious?

136
00:15:23,719 --> 00:15:28,219
She buried two husbands.
We couldn't prove anything.

137
00:15:30,319 --> 00:15:34,819
She thought they were rich. Wrong!
What's obvious about her?

138
00:15:35,359 --> 00:15:38,879
How many undercover officers?
At least ten!

139
00:15:39,159 --> 00:15:44,579
What about the blood analysis?
And are there fingerprints on the axe?

140
00:15:44,719 --> 00:15:50,112
No, none.
Check the scratches on the bumper!

141
00:15:50,679 --> 00:15:55,179
What a shame it's so busy right now.
It's Monday, after all.

142
00:15:56,359 --> 00:15:58,559
That's your office.

143
00:15:58,839 --> 00:16:03,339
Talk to the residents again!
Maybe someone saw something.

144
00:16:06,759 --> 00:16:11,259
And the guy from the
tow service! Thanks, bye!

145
00:16:11,599 --> 00:16:16,099
Nothing at Poseck's Garden. No
one saw anything, no blood traces.

146
00:16:19,039 --> 00:16:23,399
The car was parked there. And
Mrs. Hoppe was dropped off.

147
00:16:23,679 --> 00:16:28,179
No. No person fits in the
trunk. Not in one piece.

148
00:16:30,599 --> 00:16:35,099
Max, do you still have the city runabout?
Yes, why?

149
00:16:39,119 --> 00:16:41,239
It's too tight.

150
00:16:43,759 --> 00:16:47,759
What?
Oh, I see. Should we?

151
00:17:02,239 --> 00:17:06,739
It's too tight.
Try angling it more to the side!

152
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:11,759
Yes.

153
00:17:15,599 --> 00:17:20,099
I told you so.
Head back!

154
00:17:23,399 --> 00:17:27,639
Almost there.
Ouch!

155
00:17:29,759 --> 00:17:33,199
Aha! Great!

156
00:17:33,479 --> 00:17:36,239
* Lessing is knocking from inside. *

157
00:17:36,519 --> 00:17:41,019
I can't open the trunk.
Do you have a cutting torch?

158
00:17:41,759 --> 00:17:44,599
The blood belongs to Ms. Hoppe.

159
00:17:49,879 --> 00:17:54,379
The blood is Ms. Hoppe's.
It's 1.5 liters.

160
00:17:54,879 --> 00:17:59,379
She was injured outside
the trunk. That means: even more blood.

161
00:18:00,799 --> 00:18:03,199
Then she barely survived.

162
00:18:03,479 --> 00:18:07,959
That means: the perpetrator is demanding
ransom for a corpse?

163
00:18:11,199 --> 00:18:15,239
* Suspenseful music *

164
00:18:21,679 --> 00:18:26,179
The coachman again!
Caspar Bogdanski. He's harmless.

165
00:18:28,919 --> 00:18:33,419
His daughter is my brother's
ex. She turned on the desk lamp.

166
00:18:36,359 --> 00:18:40,519
Sigmar Hoppe can hit the road.
Understood.

167
00:18:57,199 --> 00:19:00,239
Yeah, go ahead and wave us off!

168
00:19:14,999 --> 00:19:19,499
The bachelors are great.
The bachelors aren't ours.

169
00:19:20,399 --> 00:19:24,899
The couple is doing
great. They're really in love.

170
00:19:26,639 --> 00:19:31,139
Stich can't find out. He doesn't
like romance in the workplace.

171
00:19:31,919 --> 00:19:36,419
Who is the father of your child?
Is he a cop too?

172
00:19:40,159 --> 00:19:43,879
He's an astrophysicist and
still lives in Berlin.

173
00:19:44,159 --> 00:19:47,399
Master or journeyman?

174
00:19:47,679 --> 00:19:52,179
He discovered a three-armed barred
spiral galaxy. It bears my name.

175
00:19:54,999 --> 00:19:59,499
(he sings) A barred spiral galaxy
that bears your name!

176
00:20:03,559 --> 00:20:07,479
Hello! Who do we have here?

177
00:20:07,759 --> 00:20:12,259
That's Olm, the head of the
Trade Registry. Forget about it!

178
00:20:16,759 --> 00:20:20,559
That's obviously fake. No one
could possibly be that stupid.

179
00:20:25,319 --> 00:20:29,819
My water is breaking.
What's her pay grade?

180
00:20:41,319 --> 00:20:44,625
Come on, come on, come on! Over here!

181
00:20:50,639 --> 00:20:55,139
Cyclists one and two, take over!
All clear! I've got it.

182
00:20:59,119 --> 00:21:03,619
* Suspenseful music *

183
00:21:20,079 --> 00:21:21,599
Everyone waits.

184
00:21:24,839 --> 00:21:28,559
Go!
Left onto Wielandstraße! Quickly!

185
00:21:32,239 --> 00:21:36,739
How did you do that?
Elevator, Lessing.

186
00:21:51,599 --> 00:21:54,079
Follow Olm! Keep your distance!

187
00:22:06,999 --> 00:22:11,499
Watch the trash cans until we're sure
we have the suspect.

188
00:22:18,239 --> 00:22:22,599
What do you want with Olm?
Did she rob a bank?

189
00:22:22,879 --> 00:22:27,379
Does the woman have a first name?
Olm?

190
00:22:30,559 --> 00:22:34,999
* Suspenseful music *

191
00:22:35,279 --> 00:22:37,319
Brrr!

192
00:22:39,639 --> 00:22:42,999
Well, bravo! That's coming off.

193
00:22:43,479 --> 00:22:47,979
This will make us famous. The money
transfer from Weimar - failed!

194
00:22:48,679 --> 00:22:50,839
What kind of money transfer?

195
00:23:01,679 --> 00:23:05,919
* Suspenseful music *

196
00:23:23,635 --> 00:23:31,255
Your wife gets a parking
sticker for the city and we'll forget about it.

197
00:23:31,279 --> 00:23:35,719
Hand over your driver's
license and we'll forget everything!

198
00:23:35,999 --> 00:23:40,199
Or should two colleagues
pick up your driver's license?

199
00:23:40,479 --> 00:23:44,479
Windmühlenstraße
14. Is that still current?

200
00:23:44,759 --> 00:23:46,679
You'll hear from me.

201
00:23:49,919 --> 00:23:53,559
Good day! Lessing.

202
00:23:53,839 --> 00:23:56,639
Olm.
Did you forget anything?

203
00:23:56,919 --> 00:23:58,199
Why?

204
00:23:58,479 --> 00:24:02,399
In your handbag.
Oh, the envelope!

205
00:24:02,679 --> 00:24:07,179
It should go to the lost and found. So much money!
Who throws stuff like that away?

206
00:24:08,679 --> 00:24:10,999
Do you have any gum?

207
00:24:13,159 --> 00:24:17,079
Are you crazy? I'm supposed to have
kidnapped Hoppe?

208
00:24:17,359 --> 00:24:21,859
You didn't know anything about the ransom?
Ransom for a corpse?

209
00:24:23,519 --> 00:24:27,319
Mrs. Hoppe is dead?
Do you want to tell us that?

210
00:24:27,599 --> 00:24:31,879
Is it a hidden camera?
She didn't want to go to the lost-and-found.

211
00:24:32,159 --> 00:24:35,999
Yes! Be glad that
my chewing gum ...

212
00:24:36,279 --> 00:24:39,519
Too stupid to throw away chewing gum?
What audacity!

213
00:24:39,799 --> 00:24:44,039
What flavor is this?
Dead Smurf?

214
00:24:44,319 --> 00:24:48,819
Watch out! In 20 minutes I have
an appointment with the mayor.

215
00:24:50,599 --> 00:24:55,099
Should I tell him that you both
are accusing me of murder?

216
00:25:04,999 --> 00:25:08,639
* Loud Laughter *

217
00:25:11,319 --> 00:25:15,819
The call to Sigmar Hoppe was
at 9.47. Where were you then?

218
00:25:17,399 --> 00:25:21,899
In a meeting for the campaign
"Weimar shimmers". The witness is Stich.

219
00:25:24,199 --> 00:25:25,559
I understand.

220
00:25:27,399 --> 00:25:30,559
You may go. You'll hear from me.

221
00:25:30,839 --> 00:25:35,339
Is the Trade Office also
responsible for hygiene at butchers?

222
00:25:36,239 --> 00:25:40,199
Yes, and?
Did you have anything to do with Mrs. Hoppe?

223
00:25:40,479 --> 00:25:44,979
No. Our contact was the son.
Things will be different now.

224
00:25:45,399 --> 00:25:49,399
Why? 
He'll probably sell.

225
00:25:49,679 --> 00:25:54,179
Why sell? 
He didn't feel like it anymore. Is that it?

226
00:26:22,319 --> 00:26:25,879
The matter is settled. Wasn't
anyone at the trash can?

227
00:26:26,159 --> 00:26:30,519
Deposit-bottle Kalli was there
and a ball landed on Marius.

228
00:26:31,439 --> 00:26:35,879
What's the status of things?
We had to let her go.

229
00:26:36,159 --> 00:26:38,679
The kidnapper could still come.

230
00:26:38,959 --> 00:26:43,459
No. He must have seen how
the envelope was taken out.

231
00:26:44,559 --> 00:26:46,959
He'll definitely reach out again.

232
00:26:47,239 --> 00:26:51,739
Mr. Hoppe! What do you
have to do with Nadine Reuter?

233
00:26:54,719 --> 00:26:59,219
Nadine Reuter gives
city tours for tourists.

234
00:27:00,799 --> 00:27:05,299
I offered her a catering concept.
And I have a bloated stomach.

235
00:27:08,519 --> 00:27:12,519
Mr. Hoppe! She stayed
overnight at your place.

236
00:27:12,799 --> 00:27:17,299
She leaves the house and right
after that the alleged kidnapper calls.

237
00:27:19,319 --> 00:27:23,819
What do you mean by that?
Mrs. Reuter doesn't want a butcher.

238
00:27:24,519 --> 00:27:29,725
She wants to shop. Not in
Weimar, but in Paris and New York.

239
00:27:30,119 --> 00:27:36,774
Watch your tone!
Do you want to sell the company?

240
00:27:36,799 --> 00:27:41,299
For that to happen, it would
first have to be mine. Better?

241
00:27:42,519 --> 00:27:43,719
Yes.

242
00:27:49,119 --> 00:27:50,719
Thank you!

243
00:27:50,999 --> 00:27:55,499
Mrs. Dorn! We have to look
for Mrs. Hoppe or her body.

244
00:27:57,479 --> 00:28:01,439
A full squad?
That would draw too much attention.

245
00:28:01,719 --> 00:28:05,479
The perpetrator still knows
nothing about us, unless ...

246
00:28:05,759 --> 00:28:10,259
Sigmar Hoppe is the perpetrator.
Is this too much for your condition?

247
00:28:11,439 --> 00:28:13,479
No!

248
00:28:13,759 --> 00:28:17,399
Is there a father to the
child who supports you?

249
00:28:17,679 --> 00:28:21,279
Mr. Stich! Boundaries!

250
00:28:21,559 --> 00:28:25,759
Private, professional.
Boundaries! Very good!

251
00:28:29,199 --> 00:28:30,679
Hans!

252
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:35,459
Can you cross-reference that with
the traces from Brigitte Hoppe's car?

253
00:28:36,279 --> 00:28:38,279
Whose is that? Sigmar's.

254
00:28:38,559 --> 00:28:42,919
There were dandruff flakes from
him on the driver's seat. Nothing else.

255
00:28:43,199 --> 00:28:45,199
You didn't have a negative.

256
00:28:45,479 --> 00:28:49,979
The mtDNA is identical to
Mrs. Hoppe, but Y chromosome.

257
00:28:50,719 --> 00:28:54,679
So that can only be...?
That's biology. Right?

258
00:28:56,039 --> 00:28:59,519
The son!
Exactly!

259
00:28:59,799 --> 00:29:04,299
Ha! So he did drive
the car after all!

260
00:29:35,919 --> 00:29:37,039
Bogdanski!

261
00:30:05,039 --> 00:30:09,539
Dad, you haven't eaten anything yet.
- I'll treat you to a big meal later!

262
00:30:11,199 --> 00:30:14,359
I reserved a table
by the window.

263
00:30:14,639 --> 00:30:18,999
What's going on? Do you want
to apologize for something again?

264
00:30:19,279 --> 00:30:23,779
I drove Kira and a colleague.
Something's up with the Hoppe case.

265
00:30:25,239 --> 00:30:29,399
It's quite possible that
it won't come to trial.

266
00:30:29,679 --> 00:30:34,179
But water damage is water damage.
No matter what happened to Hoppe.

267
00:30:46,399 --> 00:30:50,359
We need to go to Sigmar Hoppe. 
What? Why?

268
00:30:50,639 --> 00:30:54,999
He was driving the car, after
all. That could have been earlier.

269
00:30:55,279 --> 00:30:59,779
He'd be the right height.
That one too! We'll deal with him.

270
00:31:00,399 --> 00:31:04,119
Let him fend for himself.

271
00:31:04,399 --> 00:31:08,759
His city tours used to be the
most exciting ones in Weimar.

272
00:31:09,039 --> 00:31:13,539
Why exciting?
He knows a story about every wall.

273
00:31:14,159 --> 00:31:17,919
Does he also know about Anna
Amalia's and Goethe's affair?

274
00:31:18,199 --> 00:31:21,159
Lessing! Straight-A Abitur? Okay.

275
00:31:21,439 --> 00:31:25,239
Bogdanski lives in a house
that belongs to Hoppe.

276
00:31:25,519 --> 00:31:30,019
There was water damage and
Hoppe is suing for damages.

277
00:31:32,439 --> 00:31:36,939
The hearing was supposed to be
next week. It's about 35,000 euros.

278
00:31:40,399 --> 00:31:43,519
He has been driving around empty the whole time.

279
00:31:44,479 --> 00:31:47,999
He's looking for passengers.
There were some here.

280
00:31:48,999 --> 00:31:51,879
But: empty!

281
00:31:55,479 --> 00:31:59,979
His wife died two years ago.
Things have been going downhill for him ever since.

282
00:32:00,759 --> 00:32:05,259
He has nothing to lose.
See? That's what I mean.

283
00:32:05,919 --> 00:32:10,419
We're heading to Goethe's Garden House.
That's where he wrote "Iphigenia on Tauris”，

284
00:32:11,479 --> 00:32:14,879
"Egmont" and the famous
"Evening Song of the Hunter".

285
00:32:15,159 --> 00:32:19,659
It's called "Hunter's Evening Song".
- I have to go. We'll talk tonight.

286
00:32:22,825 --> 00:32:27,325
"Still and wild I creep through the field,
cocking my gun barrel."

287
00:32:27,799 --> 00:32:31,599
"Your beloved's image hovers ..."
- Mr. Bogdanski!

288
00:32:33,879 --> 00:32:38,992
Between twelve and one, you were
driving around empty on Theater Square.

289
00:32:39,085 --> 00:32:43,399
And when customers finally
came in, you turned them down.

290
00:32:44,719 --> 00:32:50,785
They were drunk. Is there
anything special to see here?

291
00:32:54,319 --> 00:32:56,359
No. What?

292
00:32:57,312 --> 00:33:01,812
It looks like you were
interested in the trash can.

293
00:33:02,039 --> 00:33:05,759
I don't understand. What
was I supposed to do?

294
00:33:06,039 --> 00:33:12,212
Brigitte Hoppe was kidnapped
and the ransom was in the trash can.

295
00:33:12,719 --> 00:33:17,039
Oh! And now you
think that it was me.

296
00:33:17,319 --> 00:33:23,352
They're going through a really hard time
right now. And the trouble with Mrs. Hoppe.

297
00:33:23,439 --> 00:33:27,639
35,000 euros! You
can't possibly afford that.

298
00:33:27,919 --> 00:33:34,045
No money for a lawyer. So
I'm hardly kidnapping anyone.

299
00:33:36,559 --> 00:33:40,839
Mrs. Dorn told me
what a fine man you are.

300
00:33:41,119 --> 00:33:47,305
The situation is difficult
and you're not a bad person.

301
00:33:47,679 --> 00:33:52,485
87.9 percent of crimes are
not committed by monsters.

302
00:33:52,679 --> 00:33:57,179
But by perfectly nice people
who are simply desperate.

303
00:33:57,839 --> 00:34:01,079
You don't even know me.

304
00:34:02,879 --> 00:34:07,079
You drove to Hoppe's to
give her a piece of your mind.

305
00:34:07,359 --> 00:34:10,959
And then things went
completely out of hand.

306
00:34:11,239 --> 00:34:15,739
You didn't mean to hurt
her, but you'd been drinking.

307
00:34:16,119 --> 00:34:18,759
Now both of you, stop it!

308
00:34:19,039 --> 00:34:23,539
Suddenly she was dead and
you were completely thrown.

309
00:34:24,199 --> 00:34:27,799
That's why you wanted
to blackmail Sigmar Hoppe.

310
00:34:28,079 --> 00:34:32,119
You have every right to, given
how terrible his mother was to you.

311
00:34:32,399 --> 00:34:36,759
Hold on! Now I'm supposed
to have killed her as well.

312
00:34:37,039 --> 00:34:39,719
Watch what you say, girl!

313
00:34:40,999 --> 00:34:42,759
Mr. Bogdanski!

314
00:34:43,039 --> 00:34:47,539
Did you load the body into
your car and dump it somewhere?

315
00:34:48,199 --> 00:34:51,679
How would you even do that?
Is it too heavy for you?

316
00:34:51,959 --> 00:34:57,558
I don't have a driver's license
Our car belongs to Lotte.

317
00:34:58,799 --> 00:35:02,119
You'd better talk to Sigmar Hoppe!

318
00:35:02,399 --> 00:35:07,638
He raced past me yesterday on the way
to the slaughterhouse. It was around eight.

319
00:35:09,325 --> 00:35:15,758
I thought he was heading over to the horses.
See? That's what I mean.

320
00:35:25,599 --> 00:35:30,099
That was actually meant for the
camper. But it's needed here now.

321
00:35:33,159 --> 00:35:36,119
The Olm, the Driver, Sigmar Hoppe!

322
00:35:36,399 --> 00:35:39,199
The Olm had the
money, but no motive.

323
00:35:39,479 --> 00:35:43,199
Bogdanski has a motive,
but no driver's license.

324
00:35:43,479 --> 00:35:45,439
Only Sigmar is a mystery.

325
00:35:45,719 --> 00:35:51,412
Everyone knows his mother thinks
he's good for nothing. Poor little sausage!

326
00:35:55,919 --> 00:35:59,319
Then let's take a look around here.

327
00:36:08,599 --> 00:36:13,099
Why should I come here?
Where can we talk in peace?

328
00:36:14,119 --> 00:36:16,759
Please, come in!

329
00:36:30,199 --> 00:36:34,599
Give me the fat Berta!
Is that a sausage, too?

330
00:36:39,538 --> 00:36:44,038
Sorry! I'm not having
my sensitive day today.

331
00:36:45,879 --> 00:36:50,379
Is this video-monitored?
Yes, because of the hygiene regulations.

332
00:36:50,799 --> 00:36:53,839
Can we take a look?
Yes.

333
00:37:09,399 --> 00:37:11,039
That's Mrs. Hoppe!

334
00:37:29,839 --> 00:37:34,592
Can we fast-forward?
Yes, with the arrow.

335
00:37:36,479 --> 00:37:38,599
Here?
Yes.

336
00:37:43,799 --> 00:37:46,479
Who do we have here?

337
00:37:48,759 --> 00:37:53,259
Apparently, nothing special.
A quiet Sunday evening?

338
00:37:57,439 --> 00:38:01,199
What was in the bag you threw away?

339
00:38:02,759 --> 00:38:04,519
Meat scraps.

340
00:38:22,919 --> 00:38:27,419
Does your mother often follow
you around with a big shopping bag?

341
00:38:28,919 --> 00:38:30,279
No.

342
00:38:30,559 --> 00:38:35,059
What did your mother's letter say?
I need to think about that.

343
00:38:38,159 --> 00:38:39,519
Yes.

344
00:38:40,799 --> 00:38:45,299
He probably doesn't remember what
the argument was about either.

345
00:38:45,679 --> 00:38:47,039
No.

346
00:38:47,319 --> 00:38:51,819
Where do the waste materials go?
Can you show us the room?

347
00:38:52,679 --> 00:38:55,799
There are lots of
containers and a downpipe.

348
00:38:58,639 --> 00:39:03,139
The waste is here. Through the
pipe, everything falls down.

349
00:39:04,399 --> 00:39:08,319
It smells awful. Not a
Hamburg fish market.

350
00:39:08,599 --> 00:39:13,099
Which container is from yesterday?
I can't tell you that.

351
00:39:14,039 --> 00:39:18,539
Now is a good moment for
your first Jungle Test.

352
00:39:21,479 --> 00:39:25,119
I was already in the car.
Please!

353
00:39:46,999 --> 00:39:51,499
This is really good stuff
for the Hoppe Special!

354
00:40:03,039 --> 00:40:07,539
I could already eat another one!
Mrs. Dorn, please!

355
00:40:18,999 --> 00:40:23,499
* Suspenseful music *

356
00:40:27,319 --> 00:40:30,319
That's an envelope!

357
00:40:33,999 --> 00:40:37,399
For Brigitte in case of my death.

358
00:40:39,599 --> 00:40:42,439
Her father has been dead for a week.

359
00:40:42,719 --> 00:40:47,219
Why did she only open the letter
yesterday? At work? On Sunday?

360
00:40:47,639 --> 00:40:51,079
She probably only found it
yesterday.

361
00:40:51,359 --> 00:40:55,859
I have a feeling about what it said. Mother
searched the whole house after that.

362
00:40:58,439 --> 00:41:02,319
What specifically?
The spice mix of the fat Hoppe.

363
00:41:02,599 --> 00:41:05,519
Only Father knew it
from his father.

364
00:41:05,799 --> 00:41:10,299
The end of the fat Hoppe! The
company is worthless without the recipe.

365
00:41:18,799 --> 00:41:20,479
Here!

366
00:41:28,799 --> 00:41:33,299
That's a whole fortune. Are you
just going to throw that in the trash?

367
00:41:33,959 --> 00:41:38,459
Maybe it's not his.
But his mother's!

368
00:41:42,119 --> 00:41:46,079
Hans, send a big
team to Hoppe's company!

369
00:41:46,359 --> 00:41:50,859
We need DNA samples and
the operation must be stopped.

370
00:41:53,639 --> 00:41:56,079
Sigmar Hoppe! His own mother!

371
00:41:56,359 --> 00:42:00,319
We only have circumstantial
evidence. He refuses to testify.

372
00:42:00,599 --> 00:42:05,099
No body, no case. That's why
he won't confess to murder.

373
00:42:06,039 --> 00:42:10,539
Exactly 100,000 euros! With
finger-prints of an old acquaintance!

374
00:42:12,519 --> 00:42:15,079
Interrogation, both of you!

375
00:42:38,639 --> 00:42:41,799
Sigmar!
What did you do?

376
00:42:45,119 --> 00:42:49,619
Actress! 
Strange! That guy with the woman!

377
00:42:51,839 --> 00:42:55,279
Do you find her attractive?
Of course not.

378
00:42:55,559 --> 00:43:00,039
But she radiates a
certain approachability.

379
00:43:00,319 --> 00:43:04,679
That could surely
morally renew some man.

380
00:43:04,959 --> 00:43:06,839
Not me!

381
00:43:07,119 --> 00:43:11,619
I bet you were
in school with her.

382
00:43:22,359 --> 00:43:25,319
Well. Everything was
actually going great.

383
00:43:26,679 --> 00:43:30,799
Junior boss, big
car, limitless cash.

384
00:43:31,079 --> 00:43:34,559
There was only one problem: Mother.

385
00:43:34,839 --> 00:43:39,339
Why did Mrs. Reuter have the money?
Mother wanted Nadine to leave.

386
00:43:41,159 --> 00:43:44,479
Was that worth 100,000 to her?
Yes.

387
00:43:46,879 --> 00:43:51,379
Why didn't you say that earlier?
You're not from here.

388
00:43:51,759 --> 00:43:52,959
No.

389
00:43:53,239 --> 00:43:57,399
When it comes to Nadine,
everyone thinks of greed and murder.

390
00:43:57,679 --> 00:44:02,159
You've already passed
judgment on me anyway.

391
00:44:02,439 --> 00:44:06,939
Wrong! But any other woman would
have left after the second dead ex.

392
00:44:09,239 --> 00:44:12,719
And you swagger around
with your proud breasts.

393
00:44:12,999 --> 00:44:17,499
You need some backbone for
that. Forgive me! My frivolous day!

394
00:44:19,199 --> 00:44:23,699
By the way, congratulations!
Finally no longer a virgin!

395
00:44:31,999 --> 00:44:36,499
The 100,000 were certainly tempting.
But you wanted everything once again.

396
00:44:40,919 --> 00:44:45,419
Nadine gave you the money. And then?
She didn't want to live with me like that.

397
00:44:48,719 --> 00:44:51,239
As long as your mother is alive!

398
00:44:57,599 --> 00:45:01,479
You crashed at his place
yesterday. He called me.

399
00:45:01,759 --> 00:45:05,279
He was arguing with his
mother and needed me.

400
00:45:05,559 --> 00:45:09,239
For what? To dispose of the body?

401
00:45:09,519 --> 00:45:14,019
And with his mother's phone
you staged a kidnapping.

402
00:45:15,839 --> 00:45:20,339
Then I say the kidnapper wants
45.000. Do you take me for a fool?

403
00:45:21,079 --> 00:45:25,579
A genius! You know about
the lawsuit with the coach driver.

404
00:45:26,279 --> 00:45:30,779
It's about a similar amount and it
was clear that we'd come across it.

405
00:45:31,799 --> 00:45:33,799
You're giving me too much credit.

406
00:45:34,079 --> 00:45:38,579
You said you never
drive your mother's car.

407
00:45:39,199 --> 00:45:42,519
How did your dandruff
end up on the headrest?

408
00:45:44,759 --> 00:45:46,399
Because ...

409
00:45:46,679 --> 00:45:51,179
I was refueling last week.
How sweet!

410
00:45:52,799 --> 00:45:57,299
You're not a butcher. Your photos
show what you were never allowed to have.

411
00:45:59,279 --> 00:46:03,599
Because of Mother. How long have
you wanted out of the company?

412
00:46:03,879 --> 00:46:08,379
It was agreed that I would study
photography after my butchery apprenticeship.

413
00:46:09,959 --> 00:46:14,459
After Father died, I told
Mother that it was time to quit.

414
00:46:17,159 --> 00:46:21,659
But for your mother, Mrs.
Reuter was the real reason.

415
00:46:23,079 --> 00:46:24,799
Yes.

416
00:46:25,079 --> 00:46:28,799
That's why Mother had
to go. At whatever cost.

417
00:46:29,079 --> 00:46:33,579
When she came with the hatchet,
you thought of a permanent solution.

418
00:46:35,159 --> 00:46:39,659
I drove away after that. I
know nothing about a hatchet.

419
00:46:40,559 --> 00:46:45,059
I haven't seen Mother again
since then. You have to believe me.

420
00:46:47,879 --> 00:46:52,379
Did she drive over to you after the fight?
You took her son away from her.

421
00:46:53,799 --> 00:46:58,199
She storms in and you
can get rid of her for good.

422
00:46:58,479 --> 00:47:02,039
You tell Sigmar,
what happened.

423
00:47:02,319 --> 00:47:06,479
You dispose of the body and
spend the night together.

424
00:47:06,759 --> 00:47:10,399
But she doesn't even
know where I live.

425
00:47:13,519 --> 00:47:18,019
Such a good match! And now it's all
gone up in smoke. Just like back then!

426
00:47:20,279 --> 00:47:25,445
Slept with the German teacher and
got held back because of French.

427
00:47:25,818 --> 00:47:32,632
I didn't do anything to you. I never took any of
your friends away from you at school.

428
00:47:32,719 --> 00:47:34,959
You simply didn't have any.

429
00:47:35,239 --> 00:47:37,999
Ms. Dorn, come here!

430
00:47:46,105 --> 00:47:52,292
No body, no prosecutor!
They'll crack eventually!

431
00:47:52,479 --> 00:47:56,979
We need to let her go. I
had a shit school life, too!

432
00:48:06,919 --> 00:48:11,419
* Melancholic music *

433
00:48:23,519 --> 00:48:25,639
Nadine!

434
00:48:29,119 --> 00:48:33,619
Please don't leave me alone!
No! That's insane!

435
00:48:39,679 --> 00:48:42,039
Can I help you?

436
00:48:44,399 --> 00:48:48,799
What do you have in mind now?
 I don't know yet.

437
00:48:49,079 --> 00:48:53,579
I'm not as smart as Kira.
I have to use what I have.

438
00:48:54,239 --> 00:48:58,519
But I always chose
the wrong men.

439
00:49:00,079 --> 00:49:04,039
Maybe you'll give me a call sometime.

440
00:49:06,439 --> 00:49:07,639
Okay!

441
00:49:14,279 --> 00:49:18,779
Oh, I see. And when is he coming back?
Okay, thanks!

442
00:49:20,159 --> 00:49:23,439
I also printed something for us.

443
00:49:24,879 --> 00:49:28,479
My rock bottom
was in 10th grade.

444
00:49:28,759 --> 00:49:32,639
Acne. Uncontrollable erections.

445
00:49:32,919 --> 00:49:36,719
Because of my
nearsightedness, no P.E. class.

446
00:49:38,799 --> 00:49:43,299
Nadine dumped
Hoppe. I just saw that.

447
00:49:44,839 --> 00:49:47,879
Are you falling for it?
That's a tactic!

448
00:49:48,159 --> 00:49:52,659
But if he ends up in prison,
his inheritance is gone.

449
00:49:56,479 --> 00:50:00,979
Yes, Ms. Reuter! Lessing here!
Right, the one from just now.

450
00:50:01,799 --> 00:50:06,299
I completely forgot to
apologize for Colleague Dorn.

451
00:50:07,799 --> 00:50:12,299
That was really ... Yeah,
she is quite a bitch.

452
00:50:13,079 --> 00:50:17,579
Absolutely, yes! No idea
who got her pregnant.

453
00:50:18,799 --> 00:50:23,299
Yeah. Oh! I think she's coming.
The floor is shaking.

454
00:50:25,799 --> 00:50:30,239
Yeah. Maybe we can continue
discussing this over dinner.

455
00:50:30,519 --> 00:50:35,019
At your place? Yeah. Today? Sure!
At eight. That works!

456
00:50:36,399 --> 00:50:40,899
Oh! A moment! Just a second!
Ms. Dorn, cake again?

457
00:50:41,759 --> 00:50:46,259
Okay. So see you this evening!
Okay. Yes, see you then!

458
00:50:46,759 --> 00:50:48,439
Okay. Ciao!

459
00:50:49,199 --> 00:50:53,699
We need to make her an offer.
Then she'll hand over Sigmar.

460
00:50:55,039 --> 00:50:59,519
How do you have her number?
She gave it to me.

461
00:50:59,799 --> 00:51:04,299
You'll be wired. If Nadine testifies
against Sigmar, that's going to happen.

462
00:51:07,559 --> 00:51:09,599
What's this?

463
00:51:10,279 --> 00:51:13,639
Matching the car scratches
against the paint file.

464
00:51:13,919 --> 00:51:18,419
The Hoppe clipped a Porsche
928. It belongs to a music professor.

465
00:51:20,079 --> 00:51:24,579
I called the university. He's been
on an Asian tour for three weeks.

466
00:51:25,319 --> 00:51:28,679
The address! Did you see the address?

467
00:51:28,959 --> 00:51:32,759
No.
Windmühlenstraße 16!

468
00:51:34,719 --> 00:51:39,219
Is it Windmühlenstraße 14?
- You'll hear from me!

469
00:51:42,559 --> 00:51:46,319
Mrs. "You-Heard-About-Me"
lives next door.

470
00:51:54,599 --> 00:51:59,099
Can't you smell it?
It's getting worse.

471
00:52:00,199 --> 00:52:02,039
What is it?

472
00:52:02,319 --> 00:52:06,819
Furry, rotten, sweetish.
With traces of a corpse.

473
00:52:09,119 --> 00:52:13,619
Were you ever a sommelier?
I thought pregnant women smelled good.

474
00:52:14,399 --> 00:52:18,899
Does that have anything to do with me?
You smell wonderful.

475
00:52:20,639 --> 00:52:23,679
Mrs. Olm lives just
around the corner.

476
00:52:28,039 --> 00:52:30,879
Mrs. Hoppe was at
your place yesterday.

477
00:52:31,159 --> 00:52:35,659
She was so angry that when
she parked, she scraped a car.

478
00:52:36,079 --> 00:52:40,579
I haven't seen Mrs. Hoppe. I
want to speak to your boss.

479
00:52:42,239 --> 00:52:45,799
He sends his regards.
Warm regards!

480
00:52:46,079 --> 00:52:50,579
What's interesting is that the trade
office issues the bratwurst stand licenses.

481
00:52:53,919 --> 00:52:58,419
They're put out to
tender. Oh, excuse me!

482
00:53:09,159 --> 00:53:13,659
I've also had a table burn
through. Those are unscrupulous fellows.

483
00:53:14,879 --> 00:53:18,359
The Hoppes have the
best locations here.

484
00:53:18,639 --> 00:53:22,599
Goethe House, Schiller Museum,
Castle, Theater Square.

485
00:53:22,879 --> 00:53:26,839
I let myself be bribed.
There's just one catch.

486
00:53:27,119 --> 00:53:31,619
I handed the tenders over
to my deputy.

487
00:53:31,959 --> 00:53:36,459
Don't arrest him! Otherwise
I'll be in hot water again!

488
00:53:42,479 --> 00:53:46,439
Mrs. Dorn, you know
this place better than I do.

489
00:53:46,719 --> 00:53:51,219
Are there any other suspects?
Simply everyone hated Hoppe.

490
00:53:53,799 --> 00:53:56,799
* Phone rings. *

491
00:53:57,079 --> 00:54:00,839
Dorn. Lotte! What is it?

492
00:54:01,119 --> 00:54:05,619
You interrogated Papa for an hour.
Are you nuts?

493
00:54:06,319 --> 00:54:11,939
He was behaving strangely.
Of course, he's always plastered!

494
00:54:12,239 --> 00:54:17,885
Poor thing! And you're still beating on him!
We're just doing our job.

495
00:54:18,239 --> 00:54:22,739
He talks a lot of nonsense!
But that he kills someone ...

496
00:54:26,279 --> 00:54:30,779
Are you still on?
I have to hang up.

497
00:54:31,679 --> 00:54:33,279
Okay.

498
00:54:36,319 --> 00:54:39,119
What? Nothing.

499
00:54:39,919 --> 00:54:42,559
Let's go, time to wire it up!

500
00:54:57,519 --> 00:54:59,919
Test!
Okay.

501
00:55:00,199 --> 00:55:04,699
Your teacher disappeared without a
trace. He must have gone to the West.

502
00:55:05,319 --> 00:55:09,819
Six years after the fall of the Wall!
How old should I be?

503
00:55:18,079 --> 00:55:20,559
* Lessing rings the doorbell. *

504
00:55:39,279 --> 00:55:43,359
Now I suppose I'll have to cancel the table
by the window.

505
00:55:43,639 --> 00:55:47,839
Hey!
- I dozed off, just for a moment.

506
00:55:49,039 --> 00:55:51,759
Yesterday on my way home.

507
00:55:53,319 --> 00:55:57,819
I thought she ran into the carriage.
- Why didn't you call the police?

508
00:56:01,239 --> 00:56:05,739
They would have definitely made me blow
into the breathalyzer. That would be our end!

509
00:56:06,599 --> 00:56:11,099
Then you call Hoppe
and demand a ransom?

510
00:56:11,759 --> 00:56:16,239
It is the just punishment for
suing us.

511
00:56:17,159 --> 00:56:21,659
There are no coincidences in the universe.
Uncontrollable forces are at work!

512
00:56:23,119 --> 00:56:26,079
There's always a Big Bang in your little corner.

513
00:56:26,359 --> 00:56:30,859
These forces wanted Hoppe to
actually do something good in the end.

514
00:56:33,879 --> 00:56:38,379
How much did you ask for?
- 45,000!

515
00:56:39,199 --> 00:56:43,699
That little? Are you an idiot?
No wonder Kira suspected you.

516
00:56:45,439 --> 00:56:49,239
That was a bit low.
- Yes.

517
00:56:49,519 --> 00:56:54,019
Maybe my plan wasn't
as elaborate as I thought.

518
00:56:56,079 --> 00:56:58,239
What do we do now?

519
00:57:04,519 --> 00:57:08,839
(Nadine) I hope you like
mushrooms. It depends where.

520
00:57:09,119 --> 00:57:11,519
In the living room.

521
00:57:15,399 --> 00:57:19,479
You can't talk to Kira.
No, that's true.

522
00:57:19,759 --> 00:57:24,039
She's losing it over me.
It's spelled "meinetwegen"!

523
00:57:24,319 --> 00:57:28,279
Yes. She's a bitch.
What a crazy bitch!

524
00:57:28,559 --> 00:57:30,759
A very crazy bitch.

525
00:57:31,039 --> 00:57:35,539
One thing up front: My two men
died a completely normal death.

526
00:57:38,279 --> 00:57:42,779
They were old and glad to
have a few good days with me.

527
00:57:43,359 --> 00:57:46,919
You have no luck with men.

528
00:57:47,199 --> 00:57:51,699
Sigmar Hoppe gets you involved
in a kidnapping and a murder.

529
00:57:52,959 --> 00:57:57,459
How did he talk you into it?
That's not how it is at all.

530
00:57:58,319 --> 00:58:02,559
Then how?
He's the first one who truly loves me.

531
00:58:02,839 --> 00:58:06,039
With him, I don't feel stupid.

532
00:58:06,319 --> 00:58:10,759
And he knows a lot and
still he listens to me.

533
00:58:12,519 --> 00:58:16,319
And it couldn't have been him.
Why not?

534
00:58:16,599 --> 00:58:21,099
When I arrived, his mother was there.
She apologized and drove off.

535
00:58:22,399 --> 00:58:25,719
Yes, in the trunk!
Damn!

536
00:58:25,999 --> 00:58:30,499
I hate it when that happens.
That's the job.

537
00:58:32,039 --> 00:58:34,719
I find that uncomfortable.

538
00:58:34,999 --> 00:58:39,499
Sigmar said he last saw his mother
at the butcher's.

539
00:58:40,719 --> 00:58:45,219
You don't have to lie to me, Mrs.
Reuter. You know it was him.

540
00:58:47,719 --> 00:58:52,039
Now you feel like
it's all your fault.

541
00:58:53,839 --> 00:58:58,339
Do you find it romantic that
someone killed his mother for you?

542
00:59:06,959 --> 00:59:09,279
* She sobs. *

543
00:59:11,199 --> 00:59:14,719
One, two, action!

544
00:59:24,559 --> 00:59:29,059
Whoa! That guy really went
and shattered the nose to bits.

545
00:59:30,199 --> 00:59:34,699
Was it me, Lotte?
Or had it already been done?

546
00:59:36,599 --> 00:59:41,099
It could have been Sigmar.
- Why Sigmar?

547
00:59:41,519 --> 00:59:46,019
I could understand him. As a
kid, his mom always left him alone.

548
00:59:47,799 --> 00:59:51,319
As an adult, he was her little sausage.

549
00:59:51,599 --> 00:59:56,099
A customer of Lischka's saw
him being led away in handcuffs.

550
00:59:58,039 --> 01:00:02,539
He was released for lack of evidence.
- Then we'll provide the evidence.

551
01:00:05,279 --> 01:00:09,519
We film Sigmar while he
buries the body.

552
01:00:09,799 --> 01:00:14,299
Dad, the body is here!
- Not yet, Lotte! Not yet!

553
01:00:16,879 --> 01:00:18,479
Plan B.

554
01:00:21,719 --> 01:00:26,219
Thank you! It was Kira's idea after all
that you call me.

555
01:00:27,159 --> 01:00:29,359
Because she hates me!

556
01:00:29,639 --> 01:00:33,519
Why exactly?
I have a photo from 11th grade.

557
01:00:33,799 --> 01:00:35,439
Oh God!

558
01:00:43,399 --> 01:00:47,519
Here it is. You don't even
look at it.

559
01:00:47,799 --> 01:00:52,299
I know what Ms. Dorn looked
like. Fantastic!

560
01:00:52,759 --> 01:00:57,259
Okay! Now I have to go.
Give me the photo back!

561
01:00:58,799 --> 01:01:01,759
* A door is closed. *

562
01:01:17,879 --> 01:01:22,379
I didn't look at it.
May I?

563
01:01:26,599 --> 01:01:29,439
Fancy a surprise visit?

564
01:01:51,919 --> 01:01:54,319
Have you found Mother?

565
01:01:54,599 --> 01:01:59,099
No. We're looking for traces, in case
you killed her here.

566
01:01:59,479 --> 01:02:02,839
Why should I let you in?

567
01:02:03,119 --> 01:02:07,619
84 percent of people who
refuse, are the perpetrators.

568
01:02:19,279 --> 01:02:21,839
Feel free to look around!

569
01:02:22,559 --> 01:02:26,639
* Suspenseful music *

570
01:02:28,159 --> 01:02:31,199
Is anyone sitting there?
Absolutely not!

571
01:02:34,559 --> 01:02:36,279
Mommy!

572
01:02:41,159 --> 01:02:44,559
She probably
always liked to sit here.

573
01:02:44,839 --> 01:02:46,959
Is she dead?

574
01:02:50,399 --> 01:02:54,519
Yes, she is dead.
Then call a doctor!

575
01:02:54,799 --> 01:02:59,299
Yes, we will. Now let's take
a look at your freezer first.

576
01:03:01,719 --> 01:03:06,219
I'll notify Stich and
forensics. Okay. Here! Come!

577
01:03:13,679 --> 01:03:16,959
Well? Do you believe me now?

578
01:03:20,119 --> 01:03:24,619
Who would benefit from
the body being found here?

579
01:03:25,799 --> 01:03:30,299
Maybe he saw you kill your
mother. A freeloader

580
01:03:30,719 --> 01:03:35,219
I didn't kill my mother!
Possibly. But what if you did?

581
01:03:37,119 --> 01:03:41,279
Then you would have gotten
rid of the body quickly.

582
01:03:41,559 --> 01:03:46,059
This is all a nightmare.
I still want to see the basement.

583
01:04:00,559 --> 01:04:05,059
"The gate gazes shut
and God and Heaven pound."

584
01:04:05,359 --> 01:04:07,319
Not "knock"!

585
01:04:07,599 --> 01:04:11,759
You are to stay by the body.
It's not going anywhere.

586
01:04:16,559 --> 01:04:21,059
Lessing!
No, it's Stramm. August Stramm.

587
01:04:40,319 --> 01:04:42,999
Plan B was garbage!

588
01:04:46,959 --> 01:04:50,439
* A police siren wails. *

589
01:05:02,879 --> 01:05:06,639
* A police siren wails. *

590
01:05:09,559 --> 01:05:13,839
None of the neighbors saw anything.
But I did!

591
01:05:20,399 --> 01:05:22,519
Okay! I'm coming!

592
01:05:24,039 --> 01:05:28,539
So? Where is the body?
Gone. We found a sugar cube.

593
01:05:32,199 --> 01:05:35,959
Then she drives
through the city. Pardon?

594
01:05:36,239 --> 01:05:39,839
The body in the
back seat. Bogdanski!

595
01:05:40,119 --> 01:05:41,479
Well then!

596
01:05:44,679 --> 01:05:47,999
Mr. Hoppe, my condolences.

597
01:05:48,279 --> 01:05:52,519
Mrs. Dorn spoke of free-
riders. What did she mean?

598
01:05:52,799 --> 01:05:57,299
Someone had hoped that you
would make the body disappear.

599
01:05:57,839 --> 01:06:01,399
And then?
They could have extorted you.

600
01:06:01,679 --> 01:06:05,159
The extortioner kidnapped the body.
Apparently!

601
01:06:05,439 --> 01:06:07,719
You stay here!

602
01:06:18,959 --> 01:06:20,319
Yes.

603
01:06:26,279 --> 01:06:29,719
Can we take a look in your
trunk, Lotte?

604
01:06:29,999 --> 01:06:33,719
Now?
Let's get it over with!

605
01:06:40,359 --> 01:06:44,239
* Suspenseful music *

606
01:07:02,279 --> 01:07:03,839
Dry.

607
01:07:08,119 --> 01:07:09,839
Wow!

608
01:07:10,119 --> 01:07:14,619
I still have my lamp, too.
It's on the desk.

609
01:07:15,199 --> 01:07:19,699
Kira! I almost belonged to your
family. Is that enough now?

610
01:07:36,879 --> 01:07:41,379
Carlos has rheumatism.
Ice is good for that.

611
01:07:44,719 --> 01:07:49,219
Your father would be turning in his
grave if he saw you here.

612
01:07:50,679 --> 01:07:55,179
My father is still alive.
I said "would" too.

613
01:08:00,639 --> 01:08:02,599
Hold on!

614
01:08:09,079 --> 01:08:13,579
There ... There's a hose that's leaking.

615
01:08:40,759 --> 01:08:45,259
* Thrilling music *

616
01:08:49,959 --> 01:08:52,679
There's a hose leaking here.

617
01:08:54,479 --> 01:08:58,979
We'll come back tomorrow with a
search warrant.

618
01:08:59,519 --> 01:09:04,019
The KT will find something, even if it's
just a hair from the Hoppe.

619
01:09:04,999 --> 01:09:06,799
Good night!

620
01:09:07,599 --> 01:09:09,479
Good night!

621
01:09:14,919 --> 01:09:18,319
I can't take it anymore!

622
01:09:25,199 --> 01:09:29,699
Oh my! Hans lives here. He goes for a walk around
that time with his farty mastiff.

623
01:09:31,759 --> 01:09:36,259
Then Stich fires me after my maternity
leave. Romance in the workplace!

624
01:09:37,879 --> 01:09:42,379
I thought we'd be alone
here. Welcome to Weimar!

625
01:09:42,919 --> 01:09:47,419
We could switch to the informal "you"
now. Everyone here uses the informal "you."

626
01:09:48,999 --> 01:09:51,959
Exactly! Yes.

627
01:09:52,239 --> 01:09:56,739
You're fine with the formal "you." 
I almost figured that.

628
01:09:59,559 --> 01:10:04,059
If this hostage-taker had done
something to you and our son ...

629
01:10:06,639 --> 01:10:10,319
I would have
killed him without hesitation.

630
01:10:17,319 --> 01:10:18,799
There!

631
01:10:20,239 --> 01:10:22,199
One, two!

632
01:10:31,039 --> 01:10:35,539
Good that you're here! I just
confessed everything to Lotte.

633
01:10:36,319 --> 01:10:40,819
She didn't know anything. She said,
we have to call the police.

634
01:10:41,759 --> 01:10:46,259
I did that too.
But the line was busy.

635
01:11:05,039 --> 01:11:08,559
Mrs. Olm wants to take
my chauffeur's license away.

636
01:11:08,839 --> 01:11:12,599
The licenses are limited.
She's cashing in on it.

637
01:11:12,879 --> 01:11:17,199
Dad is her victim.
- Because I supposedly have a drinking problem.

638
01:11:17,479 --> 01:11:21,359
Everyone drinks when they're upset.
- Or when it's cold!

639
01:11:21,639 --> 01:11:25,199
Or on a Monday.
Or when a body needs to be gotten rid of.

640
01:11:25,959 --> 01:11:30,459
Did you kill Mrs. Hoppe?
No. He ran over her in his sleep.

641
01:11:31,559 --> 01:11:33,959
* Crash *

642
01:11:35,239 --> 01:11:38,159
Up at Lindenberg. Sunday night.

643
01:11:38,439 --> 01:11:42,079
He woke up, but the Hoppe
was already dead before.

644
01:11:46,999 --> 01:11:51,499
And in a flash he hatched a plan.
He wants ransom for the corpse.

645
01:11:54,919 --> 01:11:59,419
Then he noticed us and wanted
to kill two birds with one stone.

646
01:12:02,919 --> 01:12:07,419
45.000 in the trash can at the theater
for a lifetime coachman's license.

647
01:12:10,959 --> 01:12:13,399
That was no coincidence.

648
01:12:13,679 --> 01:12:17,159
The Olm was supposed
to reach into the trash can.

649
01:12:19,199 --> 01:12:23,699
Not bad! Olm should have paid
45,000 to renew her license.

650
01:12:26,319 --> 01:12:30,819
Olm should be locked up,
so you can have your peace.

651
01:12:31,559 --> 01:12:35,799
Attempted bribery, extortion.


652
01:12:36,079 --> 01:12:40,579
What did he do to Ms. Hoppe?
Disturbing the dead, concealment.

653
01:12:41,759 --> 01:12:46,259
Withholding evidence,
obstruction of justice.

654
01:12:52,519 --> 01:12:54,479
Papa!

655
01:12:58,199 --> 01:12:59,839
Respect!

656
01:13:09,879 --> 01:13:14,379
What do we do with Olm now?
She'll be hearing from us.

657
01:13:17,919 --> 01:13:22,419
How's it looking?
Severe occipital wound.

658
01:13:23,239 --> 01:13:26,639
She bled for a
long time.

659
01:13:26,919 --> 01:13:30,919
But it doesn't necessarily
have to have been fatal.

660
01:13:31,199 --> 01:13:35,239
But that should have been
enough: strangulation marks.

661
01:13:35,519 --> 01:13:38,439
What was the weapon here?

662
01:13:38,719 --> 01:13:43,219
I might know after the
autopsy. So, tomorrow.

663
01:13:43,519 --> 01:13:46,359
You mean in two hours.

664
01:13:46,639 --> 01:13:50,279
Are you the new guy from Hamburg?
Yes. Lessing.

665
01:13:50,559 --> 01:13:52,439
Can I just ...

666
01:14:04,759 --> 01:14:07,319
Hooray, the letter!

667
01:14:09,199 --> 01:14:13,699
Frozen, thawed, frozen, thawed!
The death of the fat Hoppe!

668
01:14:14,759 --> 01:14:19,259
What if this isn't the
sausage recipe at all?

669
01:14:19,759 --> 01:14:24,079
Then the letter was the reason
why she took the fat Berta.

670
01:14:24,359 --> 01:14:27,959
It leads us to the
murderer. If we can read it.

671
01:14:28,239 --> 01:14:32,739
I know who can reconstruct it:
the one at the "Anna Amalia!"

672
01:14:36,159 --> 01:14:37,719
Heads up!

673
01:14:39,959 --> 01:14:43,959
Stefan, it's Kira! Do you have
anything going on tonight?

674
01:14:44,239 --> 01:14:48,739
Stone cold. I have a letter
here with water damage.

675
01:14:50,039 --> 01:14:54,539
How fast can you get it done?
You're the best. I'll send it over.

676
01:14:56,039 --> 01:14:57,799
Bye!

677
01:14:58,719 --> 01:15:01,399
See you tomorrow too. Wow!

678
01:15:01,679 --> 01:15:05,439
We need to call the boss.
I've already done that.

679
01:15:13,639 --> 01:15:18,139
Sigmar Hoppe is taken into custody overnight.
The coachman too.

680
01:15:19,279 --> 01:15:23,779
And secures the forest path to
Lindenberg until the K9 unit arrives!

681
01:15:25,159 --> 01:15:27,839
* The cat hisses. *

682
01:15:28,919 --> 01:15:30,639
Sigmar!

683
01:15:30,919 --> 01:15:35,419
I can't sleep. I keep
thinking about how it was for me.

684
01:15:37,679 --> 01:15:42,179
People thought I had killed two people.
But there is the presumption of innocence.

685
01:15:44,519 --> 01:15:49,019
Everyone is considered innocent until
legal proof of guilt is established.

686
01:15:49,759 --> 01:15:53,519
That also applies to the press.
I love you too.

687
01:16:19,599 --> 01:16:21,599
Good morning!

688
01:16:21,879 --> 01:16:25,519
Chic!
Thank you! Weimar shimmers!

689
01:16:25,799 --> 01:16:30,299
All department heads are taking part.
Stich is also in the photo.

690
01:16:30,719 --> 01:16:35,219
Let's hurry! I was already done
with Mrs. Hoppe at seven.

691
01:16:36,559 --> 01:16:38,599
That was in the wound.

692
01:16:38,879 --> 01:16:43,379
A nice dick! Maybe a
piece of a glass vase.

693
01:16:44,919 --> 01:16:46,719
And something else.

694
01:16:46,999 --> 01:16:48,319
Here!

695
01:16:51,799 --> 01:16:54,239
This could be gold.

696
01:16:58,199 --> 01:17:02,159
And the glass shard
the edge of a tabletop?

697
01:17:02,439 --> 01:17:03,919
Possible.

698
01:17:06,039 --> 01:17:10,539
This isn't gold. It's
brass, Lessing!

699
01:17:16,719 --> 01:17:18,639
Bye!

700
01:17:35,519 --> 01:17:40,019
Whoa! So, I can smell it too now.
Man!

701
01:17:50,359 --> 01:17:54,859
The marten clearly
hit a car.

702
01:17:57,159 --> 01:17:59,439
A suicide.

703
01:18:01,719 --> 01:18:04,479
Crash through the window!

704
01:18:10,399 --> 01:18:13,879
* Police siren sounds. *

705
01:18:22,399 --> 01:18:25,359
* Police siren *

706
01:18:37,879 --> 01:18:41,559
Oh! I think the marten has gotten through.

707
01:18:41,839 --> 01:18:45,239
We're pursuing a black station wagon,
Wagner Lane!

708
01:19:24,759 --> 01:19:28,599
Pardon! Excuse me!

709
01:19:34,319 --> 01:19:36,199
Pardon!

710
01:19:44,079 --> 01:19:48,579
* Suspenseful music *

711
01:20:01,879 --> 01:20:04,279
Excuse me! Pardon!

712
01:20:22,239 --> 01:20:26,639
* Suspenseful music *

713
01:21:13,399 --> 01:21:15,679
Weapon down!

714
01:21:20,039 --> 01:21:22,399
This will never work between us!
What?

715
01:21:22,679 --> 01:21:27,179
I won't marry a wimp.
Marry?

716
01:21:29,719 --> 01:21:35,165
If it's to be, then it's to be done right!
With all the trimmings: horse, carriage, dress!

717
01:21:35,325 --> 01:21:37,119
Crown.

718
01:21:37,399 --> 01:21:43,065
She's always dreamed of that.
Me too.

719
01:21:43,799 --> 01:21:48,299
He's a true romantic.
I will shoot for real.

720
01:21:50,679 --> 01:21:54,959
You're not making me a widow.
You won't shoot.

721
01:21:55,239 --> 01:21:59,559
82 percent of such cases
end without bloodshed.

722
01:21:59,839 --> 01:22:04,339
Nonsense! You haven't
read a single statistic yet.

723
01:22:05,079 --> 01:22:09,579
I get through in 99 percent of
cases. The Hoppe ruined my life.

724
01:22:14,199 --> 01:22:15,599
All good!

725
01:22:22,679 --> 01:22:27,179
She rang the bell, I opened the
door and she came at me with an axe.

726
01:22:28,719 --> 01:22:32,479
She slammed into the
table. It was self-defense.

727
01:22:32,759 --> 01:22:37,259
Blood everywhere. She had
bled like a pig.

728
01:22:38,159 --> 01:22:42,659
That's why you didn't call the police.
The bitch had to be gotten rid of.

729
01:22:43,199 --> 01:22:46,239
You shoved her into
the trunk.

730
01:22:47,359 --> 01:22:50,959
Later, you saw that
the bitch was still alive.

731
01:22:53,999 --> 01:22:56,639
Then you strangled her.

732
01:23:02,079 --> 01:23:05,759
Yes.
But that's not self-defense. Right?

733
01:23:07,999 --> 01:23:12,199
So what is it? Why then?

734
01:23:13,199 --> 01:23:16,119
I have the letter.
She confessed.

735
01:23:24,119 --> 01:23:27,119
"Brigitte! If you're
reading this, I'm dead."

736
01:23:27,399 --> 01:23:31,899
"I can't tell you the
recipe for the fat bitch."

737
01:23:32,479 --> 01:23:36,979
"You know I only ever loved
one woman. It wasn't you."

738
01:23:37,839 --> 01:23:42,239
"Sigmar doesn't want the
company and you don't deserve it."

739
01:23:42,519 --> 01:23:47,019
"I leave the recipe to
my beloved Karin. Fuck it!"

740
01:23:48,919 --> 01:23:50,439
Karin?

741
01:23:52,319 --> 01:23:56,199
That's no big deal. Karin Olm!

742
01:23:58,199 --> 01:24:01,359
They have the recipe
for the Fat Hoppe.

743
01:24:02,679 --> 01:24:07,179
The recipe is at home in the envelope.
On the outside it said:

744
01:24:08,959 --> 01:24:11,359
"Dear Karin!"

745
01:24:11,639 --> 01:24:15,159
"No fire, no coal,
can burn so hot ..."

746
01:24:15,439 --> 01:24:19,599
"Like a secret, quiet love, of
which no one knows a thing."

747
01:24:27,239 --> 01:24:31,739
* Romantic piano music *

748
01:25:12,479 --> 01:25:15,999
Boss!
We have something to tell you.

749
01:25:16,279 --> 01:25:18,519
I already know.

750
01:25:20,919 --> 01:25:25,419
Make two more! The Fat-Hoppe
recipe was in the Olms' apartment.

751
01:25:26,759 --> 01:25:31,259
Sigmar is selling the company, but
the sausage will still be produced.

752
01:25:32,039 --> 01:25:34,759
Good work, colleagues!

753
01:25:38,559 --> 01:25:39,719
Thanks!

754
01:25:39,999 --> 01:25:44,159
We can also reveal the recipe
for the Fat Dorn.

755
01:25:44,439 --> 01:25:46,119
Mr. Lessing!

756
01:25:46,399 --> 01:25:50,899
Boundaries! Professional,
Personal! Boundaries!

757
01:26:00,439 --> 01:26:04,939
Subtitle:
Line 21 / Frank H. Richter

